# Rules are evaluated last-match-wins, so the `patchlets/` rule must stay last.

# The repository is LF throughout. Pin it so a Windows clone with the default
# core.autocrlf=true does not check files out as CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary payloads: never diffed, never EOL-converted.
*.apk  binary
*.jar  binary
*.so   binary
*.dex  binary
*.gz   binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.mp4  binary
*.zip  binary

# The canonical tree is hash-pinned. resolution.json records SHA-256 hashes of
# 46 assets under patchlets/, several as whole-tree digests with filter '*'
# (patchlets/assets/socks5-proxy/native and the block-list fixture tree), and
# the pipeline re-hashes them as a precondition. Any EOL conversion here changes
# the bytes, so the hash check fails and the build stops -- reporting APK drift
# rather than a line-ending problem. Store and check out these bytes verbatim.
patchlets/** -text
